-- A deliberate ENCODING DEFECT, kept as the positive control for R-V5's replay.
-- A record passed to another rule is lowered as if every field were read, so
-- the encoding believes the call below raises when p is 0. The evaluator is
-- lazy, never reads that field, and says TRUE there. `l4 prove` must report
-- the disagreement as a defect in itself, never as a counterexample.
DECLARE Item
  HAS price IS A NUMBER
      paid  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN i IS AN Item
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is paid` i MEANS i's paid

§ `Lazy fields`
    GIVEN p IS A NUMBER

#ASSERT p GREATER THAN 0 OR `is paid` (Item OF (1 DIVIDED BY p), p AT MOST 0)
